  "root_cause_analysis": {
    "summary": "The ART loader reads attacker-controlled header bytes from an RBuffer into ao->art and stores parsed metadata in ao->kv. load_buffer then registers ao->kv under the parent Sdb namespace, so namespace/core cleanup will later manage that Sdb pointer. The vulnerable ART plugin destroy path nevertheless calls sdb_free(obj->kv). That premature free leaves the namespace ownership path with a stale Sdb pointer, and later cleanup calls sdb_free again; the second call dereferences the already freed Sdb fields and ASan reports heap-use-after-free.",
    "key_mechanism": "ownership_transfer_followed_by_plugin_free_and_later_namespace_double_free",
    "why_patch_works": "The patch removes sdb_free(obj->kv) from the ART plugin destroy path. Because ao->kv has been registered under the parent namespace, leaving the Sdb lifetime to the namespace/core owner prevents the premature free and the later cleanup no longer dereferences freed Sdb memory."
  },
